# Batch launchers must keep CRLF line endings in every checkout (cmd.exe).
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Shipped skill files are byte-identity-anchored: the pre-#151 migration
# (SKILL_MIGRATION_PLAN in scripts/pi-review-gate-launcher.cjs) proves a
# prior generic copy is package-owned only by exact-byte identity against
# the recorded LF historical digests, and the npm tarball ships these files
# as LF. Windows checkouts default to core.autocrlf=true, which would turn
# the packaged sources into CRLF and fail the digest anchor (fail-closed
# preservation, PR 169 Windows launcher CI); pinning LF keeps the packaged
# bytes canonical in every checkout on every platform.
skills/**/*.md text eol=lf
